<title>FRANCE: Eurotunnel shares ease on TML decision.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel shares ease on TML decision.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Eurotunnel underperformed the bourse on Tuesday after the Channel Tunnel operator said it received a mixed decision in its long-running conflict with rolling stock manufacturer TML.</p>
<p>Eurotunnel shares were down 1.49 percent at 6.60 francs at 0925 GMT while the bourse's CAC-40 index was 0.74 percent lower.</p>
<p>Eurotunnel said a panel of experts said it was entitled to damages for deficiencies in some rolling stock and urged the parties to negotiate appropriate compensation but rejected Eurotunnel's demands relating to losses in revenue.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
